## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-world ability to build autonomous, tool-using planning with LangChain, handling failures and idempotence under latency.

## Key Concepts

- LangChain Tools orchestration
- Planning/Autogen style decomposition
- Idempotence and retry semantics
- Observability and testing strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal pseudoplanner
async function planIncident(incident, tools){
  const steps = [];
  if (incident.severity>3) steps.push({name:'fetchMetrics', tool:'metrics_api'});
  steps.push({name:'lookupRunbook', tool:'runbooks_db'});
  steps.push({name:'ensureTicket', tool:'ticket_api'});
  return steps;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test decision paths across edge cases?
- How would you extend to parallel tool execution when safe?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to craft a robust, end-to-end evaluation pipeline for multilingual policy-faithfulness in a high-stakes financial setting, with versioned source control and drift monitoring.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual claim extraction and anchor mapping
- Versioned source citations and live policy integration
- Drift detection and change management across monthly updates

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal citation check
function checkCitation(claim, citation, policyDB) {
  const live = policyDB.lookup(citation.version, citation.id);
  return live && live.text.includes(claim.anchor);
}
```
